questions.answer:
7 {'_Secret__val': 7}
7

Inside the property methods, self.__val mangles to self._Secret__val, so the setter and getter transparently read and write the mangled slot even though they live in different functions of the same class. s.value = 7 goes through the property setter and stores 7 under the mangled key; s.value reads it back. Accessing s._Secret__val directly proves the attribute really lives under the mangled name.

